P3 (design §4.3): /etc/ld.so.preload -> /etc/ld-nix.so.preload, so a host
preload file never injects host DSOs into processes of the relocated glibc
(same name as nixpkgs: NixOS's environment.etc."ld-nix.so.preload" works).
Rebased from nixpkgs 26f4107e47e3 pkgs/development/libraries/glibc/dont-use-system-ld-so-preload.patch
onto Rocky glibc-2.39-142.el10_2 after %prep; same change, no others.

--- a/elf/rtld.c
+++ b/elf/rtld.c
@@ -1892,7 +1892,7 @@
      open().  So we do this first.  If it succeeds we do almost twice
      the work but this does not matter, since it is not for production
      use.  */
-  static const char preload_file[] = "/etc/ld.so.preload";
+  static const char preload_file[] = "/etc/ld-nix.so.preload";
   if (__glibc_unlikely (__access (preload_file, R_OK) == 0))
     {
       /* Read the contents of the file.  */
